  "question": {
    "text": "The family of straight lines \\((2 a+3 b) x+(a-b) y+2 a-4 b=0\\) is concurrent at the point"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\\(\\left(\\frac{2}{5}, \\frac{-14}{5}\\right)\\)",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\left(\\frac{-2}{5}, \\frac{-14}{5}\\right)\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\left(\\frac{-2}{5}, \\frac{14}{5}\\right)\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\left(\\frac{2}{5}, \\frac{14}{5}\\right)\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Rewriting the equation \\((2 x+y+2) a+(3 x-y-4) b=0\\) and for all \\(a\\), \\(\\mathrm{b}\\) the straight lines pass through the intersection of \\(2 x+y+2=0\\) and \\(3 x-y-4=0\\) i.e., the point \\(\\left(\\frac{2}{5},-\\frac{14}{5}\\right)\\)."
  }
}